 "handle": "http://www.youtube.com/@electricianron_New_Jersey",
 "description": "My name is Ron Pecina, owner of Classic Electric of Point Pleasant, New Jersey. This page is about electrical work and the work that my business offers.  I have been an electrician since 1990 when I enlisted in the United States Navy and became a Construction Electrician in the Seabees. This is how I got my start in this industry and I am proud to be a professional in this business. After nineteen years and working for several electrical contractors in the Westfield, Cranford, and Clark area, I decided to earn my state electrical license and business permit.  In 2009,  Classic Electric, LLC. became a reality and I've been doing the kind of work you'll be seeing in these videos ever since. \n\nI'm an active member in the New Jersey Independent Electrical Contractors association (NJ-IEC) and an electrical instructor for our approved apprenticeship program in Somerset, New Jersey. \n\nLike, subscribe, comment, and share! \n\nThank you! \n\nRon Pecina Jr.\n",
